  "id": "Compound::DB01199 - Gene::1129",
  "verbalization": "Tubocurarine is linked to Chrm2 through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately involve the acetylcholine receptor. The evidence suggests that Tubocurarine binds to a receptor-like entity (Chrnd, Chrnb1, or Chrna2), which then participates in acetylcholine receptor activity. This activity is ultimately associated with Chrm2, indicating a pathway where Tubocurarine may influence the function of the acetylcholine receptor complex. The varying binding targets (Chrnd, Chrnb1, and Chrna2) suggest that Tubocurarine interacts with different subunits of the acetylcholine receptor, potentially modulating its activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism by which Tubocurarine could affect Chrm2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
